<p>The basics, in order. Every video goes through the same ten steps; nothing here repeats what the</p>
<p>Final Cut templates do — it says <em>when</em> to reach for them.</p>
<h2>0 · Start a project folder</h2>
<p>Copy a project folder and rename it <code>YYYY-MM-DD-short-name</code> (e.g. <code>2026-11-20-lisbon-day-3</code>).</p>
<pre><code>
01-footage/      camera + phone clips, straight off the card — never rename inside
02-audio/        mic recordings, voice-over
03-music-sfx/    the music bed and sound effects you used (copied, so the project travels)
04-graphics/     screenshots, logos, anything you made for this video
05-thumbnail/    the thumbnail file + 2 alternatives
06-exports/      final video, Shorts cut-downs, captions file
CHECKLIST.md     tick it off as you go
</code></pre>
<h2>1 · Plan (10 minutes, before you film)</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>One promise.</b> Finish the sentence "After watching this, you'll…". If you can't, don't film yet.</li>
<li><b>Title and thumbnail first.</b> Write the title and sketch the thumbnail word now — the video should deliver what they promise. Pick the thumbnail type and series from design.imswarnil.com › Concept › Thumbnails.</li>
<li><b>Shot list:</b> opening line (first 5 seconds), 3–5 beats, the ending, 10 B-roll shots.</li>
</ul>
<h2>2 · Shoot</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Phone:</b> 4K 30 fps (talking) or 1080p 60 fps (motion). Lock exposure and focus (long-press). Clean the lens.</li>
<li><b>Light:</b> face a window; never a window behind you.</li>
<li><b>Sound beats picture:</b> a clip-on mic. Record 10 seconds of silence in every location (room tone — it hides cuts).</li>
<li><b>B-roll:</b> every shot 5+ seconds, steady, three angles of the same thing (wide, medium, close).</li>
<li><b>Clap</b> once on camera when you start a second recorder — it lines the sound up later.</li>
</ul>
<h2>3 · Import (Final Cut Pro)</h2>
<ul>
<li>One <b>Library per series</b> (Daily vlog, Travel, Tutorials…), one <b>Event per video</b>.</li>
<li>Import from <code>01-footage</code> with <em>Leave files in place</em> — the project folder is the archive.</li>
<li>Keywords while you watch: <code>good</code>, <code>b-roll</code>, <code>funny</code>, <code>talking</code>. Then filter by <code>good</code>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>4 · Edit — three passes</h2>
<ul>
<li><b>Selects:</b> only the best takes on the timeline, in order. Too long is fine.</li>
<li><b>Story:</b> cut it to the promise. Remove every sentence that doesn't serve it. The first 30 seconds get the most cuts.</li>
<li><b>Polish:</b> J- and L-cuts (sound starts before the picture), B-roll over jump cuts, pacing.</li>
</ul>
<p>Then, and only then, reach for the templates (Titles / Transitions / Generators / Effects in Final Cut):</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Opener / chapter / quote / stat / recap / outro</b> → <em>Im Design - Scenes</em></li>
<li><b>Freeze frame + name</b> → <em>Im Design - Freeze</em></li>
<li><b>Words on screen</b> → <em>Im Design - Text FX</em> · thumbnail-style parts → <em>Im Design - Poster</em></li>
<li><b>Between scenes</b> → <em>Im Design - Page Cuts / Pro Cuts</em> — one transition style per video, not a different one every cut</li>
<li><b>Music visualizer</b> → the visualizer maker</li>
</ul>
<h2>5 · Sound</h2>
<ul>
<li>Dialogue peaks around −6 dB, the whole mix about <b>−14 LUFS</b> (YouTube's loudness).</li>
<li>Music bed under talking at roughly <b>−20 to −24 dB</b>; let it rise in gaps.</li>
<li>Sound effects from the sound library — a whoosh on a cut, a pop on a title. Fewer is better.</li>
<li>Room tone under every cut in talking scenes.</li>
</ul>
<h2>6 · Colour</h2>
<ul>
<li>Fix first: exposure and white balance per clip so skin matches across clips.</li>
<li>Then the look: Effects › Color › <b>Custom LUT</b> › <code>Im - Signature</code> at 80–100% on an adjustment layer over everything.</li>
<li>Leave the red (#f22f46) red. Titles are added after the grade, never graded.</li>
</ul>
<h2>7 · Captions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Final Cut: <em>Edit › Captions › Transcribe to Captions</em> (or upload to YouTube and fix its auto captions).</li>
<li>Short lines, no more than two at a time. Check every name and number.</li>
</ul>
<h2>8 · Thumbnail</h2>
<ul>
<li>Pixelmator template (same series as the video), <b>or</b> on the phone with its PNG layer pack and Geist — see Layers &amp; LUTs.</li>
<li>Make the word + 2 alternatives; save to <code>05-thumbnail/</code>. Check it at the size of your thumb.</li>
</ul>
<h2>9 · Export</h2>
<div class="im-table-scroll"><table><tbody>
<tr><td>For</td><td>Settings (File › Share › Export File)</td></tr>
<tr><td>YouTube</td><td>4K (or source size), H.264 or HEVC, "Better quality", 30/60 fps as shot</td></tr>
<tr><td>Shorts / Reels</td><td>1080 × 1920, separate project (9:16), max 60–90 s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Archive</td><td>Apple ProRes 422 of the master — keep it in <code>06-exports/</code></td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<h2>10 · Publish</h2>
<ul>
<li>Title (the promise, under 60 characters) · description (first 2 lines matter) · chapters (<code>00:00 Intro</code> …)</li>
<li>Thumbnail · end screen (Outro scene, 20 s) · cards to one related video</li>
<li>Captions uploaded · 3–5 specific tags · playlist = the series</li>
<li>After 48 hours: check click-through and where people leave; write one line in <code>CHECKLIST.md</code> for next time.</li>
</ul>
<p><b>On the phone only</b> (no Mac): CapCut or VN for the edit (both import the <code>.cube</code> LUTs), PicsArt for the thumbnail with the layer packs, the same ten steps.</p>
